2b20a595a219dc31b1591f6477?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-10T17:50:27.929Z"},{"id":"RumuRfVon","title":"All JavaScript and TypeScript Features of the last 3 years","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/all-javascript-and-typescript-features-of-the-last-3-years-629c57e73e42?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/all-javascript-and-typescript-features-of-the-last-3-years-rumurfvon","summary":"This post covers all the JavaScript and TypeScript features of the last 3 years, showcasing the changes in the languages. It discusses features like tagged template literals, symbols, optional chaining, nullish coalescing operator, dynamically import, string.matchAll, Promise.any, BigInt, globalThis, import.meta, and many more.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7d487a16946a51156579abbe1c24f6f3?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-08T13:11:12.761Z"},{"id":"sqbzQVJtQ","title":"What I Hope to See for SwiftUI at WWDC 2023","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/what-i-hope-to-see-for-swiftui-at-wwdc-2023-fcf409e2d874?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-i-hope-to-see-for-swiftui-at-wwdc-2023-sqbzqvjtq","summary":"List of desired features for SwiftUI at WWDC 2023, including view association with attribute granularity, unified gesture logic, more complete text input and display, stable ForEach implementation, and forward compatibility.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/035c399fbcb4c089185fea2fe9a133a5?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-27T23:28:09.173Z"},{"id":"RKq6kmZfn","title":"Let a thousand programming publications bloom.","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/let-a-thousand-programming-publications-bloom-bf37baef8f27?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/let-a-thousand-programming-publications-bloom--rkq6kmzfn","summary":"The author is putting Better Programming on hiatus to make room for other programming publications. They encourage readers to start their own publications and provide guidelines on how to do it well. They highlight the importance of focus, community-building, expertise, and recruitment of authors. They also emphasize that while there may be financial rewards, the main benefit is portfolio-building.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/cc08c4cda02f48897ba225e8929753fc?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-10T20:03:29.708Z"},{"id":"anrM4pORi","title":"What If Java Collections Had Eager Methods for Filter, Map, FlatMap?","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/what-if-java-collections-had-eager-methods-for-filter-map-flatmap-a61ef07fa52a?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-if-java-collections-had-eager-methods-for-filter-map-flatmap--anrm4pori","summary":"The article explores the use of advanced Java language features, such as covariant return types, default and static methods on interfaces, and sealed classes, to enhance the Java Collections framework. It introduces eager iteration patterns in Java Collections and discusses the benefits and possibilities they offer. It also explores the implementation of immutable collection types using sealed classes. The article provides code examples and demonstrations of the experimental collections framework.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/bbed6067f15ce82d74fb36bb51b5d721?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-10T17:20:51.248Z"},{"id":"9bYylqq5C","title":"System Design Series: ElasticSearch, Architecting for search","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/system-design-series-elasticsearch-architecting-for-search-5d5e61360463?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/system-design-series-elasticsearch-architecting-for-search-9byylqq5c","summary":"This article provides an introduction to how Elasticsearch works and its architecture. It explains the complexity of full-text search and the challenges it poses. The article also covers the terminology used in Elasticsearch, such as nodes, indexes, documents, and shards. It explains how shards work and the concept of primary and replica shards. Finally, it discusses how search and query by ID queries are performed in Elasticsearch.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/099234fdb5b97fcd6a615d742022647f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-25T13:41:36.055Z"},{"id":"kJ21kCENA","title":"How I Fell in Kotlin\u2019s RunBlocking Deadlock Trap, and How You Can Avoid It","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/how-i-fell-in-kotlins-runblocking-deadlock-trap-and-how-you-can-avoid-it-db9e7c4909f1?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-i-fell-in-kotlin-s-runblocking-deadlock-trap-and-how-you-can-avoid-it-kj21kcena","summary":"The runBlocking function in Kotlin coroutines can lead to a deadlock if called from the wrong thread. To avoid this, it is recommended to use custom coroutine scopes or take a top-down approach when migrating to coroutines. The article shares the author's experience with runBlocking and provides insights on avoiding the deadlock trap.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/77f83aa434a1f27a821671a4c6b080cd?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-25T12:55:49.380Z"},{"id":"j1OuCtdvf","title":"Why DSA Interviews Are Great for Recruiting \u2014 My Experience With Meta","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/why-dsa-interviews-are-great-for-recruiting-my-experience-with-meta-b970eb867a4a?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-dsa-interviews-are-great-for-recruiting-my-experience-with-meta-j1ouctdvf","summary":"DSA interviews can help engineers improve their skills and progress in their careers. A good grasp of DSA can lead to building efficient systems. Communication and problem-solving are important in DSA interviews and in day-to-day work as an engineer.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/50c3c349b6b851a36a2b2008d021a589?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-18T19:47:38.318Z"},{"id":"fJjTDTuOU","title":"Hack Your Next Interview with Generative AI","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/hack-your-next-interview-with-generative-ai-fb8c8bc3cbce?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/hack-your-next-interview-with-generative-ai-fjjtdtuou","summary":"An article discusses how to build a small application using Whisper for voice recognition and ChatGPT for text generation to assist in job interviews. It covers capturing speaker audio, speech-to-text conversion, answer generation, and creating a simple GUI using PySimpleGUI.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c2eeda5433038bcabfb0a6e8c8ddfac7?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":11,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-12T17:29:14.462Z"},{"id":"YNvSkL03T","title":"Understanding Digital Identity, Encryption, and OAuth 2.0 vs OIDC","url":"https://betterprogramming.pub/understanding-digital-identity-encryption-and-oauth-2-0-vs-oidc-b23381f5cdc6?source=rss----d0b105d10f0a---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/understanding-digital-identity-encryption-and-oauth-2-0-vs-oidc-ynvskl03t","summary":"This article explores the concepts of digital identity, encryption, and the differences between OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect. It also discusses the various types of tokens used for access and identity.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dc8367dff5164317c78fb4e5c7cee549?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-10T23:02